{"comments":"Nurbs — Non-Uniform Rational B-Splines for professional curve modeling.\n\n## Design Philosophy\n\nNURBS are the gold standard for precise curve and surface representation\nin CAD, professional animation, and industrial design. They extend B-splines\nwith two key features:\n\n- **Weights**: Each control point has a weight that affects how strongly\n  it \"pulls\" the curve. Weights enable exact representation of conic\n  sections (circles, ellipses, hyperbolas).\n\n- **Non-uniform knots**: The knot vector can have non-uniform spacing,\n  allowing finer control over where the curve \"responds\" to control points.\n\n## Mathematical Foundation\n\nA NURBS curve of degree p is defined as:\n\n```\nC(u) = Σᵢ (Nᵢ,ₚ(u) · wᵢ · Pᵢ) / Σᵢ (Nᵢ,ₚ(u) · wᵢ)\n```\n\nWhere:\n- Pᵢ are control points\n- wᵢ are weights (positive numbers)\n- Nᵢ,ₚ(u) are B-spline basis functions of degree p\n- The knot vector determines the basis functions\n\n## Key Properties\n\n- **Exact conics**: Circles, ellipses, and arcs can be represented exactly\n- **Local control**: Moving one point affects only nearby curve segments\n- **Affine invariance**: Transformations apply to control points only\n- **Variation diminishing**: The curve is \"smoother\" than control polygon\n\n## Use Cases\n\n- CAD/CAM systems (Solidworks, AutoCAD, Rhino)\n- Typography and font design\n- Aircraft and automotive body design\n- Professional 3D modeling (Maya, Blender)\n- CNC machining tool paths\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Schema.Geometry.Point (Point2D for control points)\n- Schema.Geometry.Vector (Vector2D for tangents)\n- Data.Array (control points, knots, weights)\n","declarations":[{"children":[{"comments":null,"info":{"arguments":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Prim"],"Record"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["controlPoints",{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Prim"],"Array"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Geometry","Nurbs"],"ControlPoint"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["knots",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Geometry","Nurbs"],"KnotVector"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["degree",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Prim"],"Int"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"tag":"REmpty"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}],"declType":"dataConstructor"},"sourceSpan":{"end":[188,4],"name":"src/Hydrogen/Schema/Geometry/Nurbs.purs","start":[184,20]},"title":"NurbsCurve"},{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Eq"],"Eq"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Geometry","Nurbs"],"NurbsCurve"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[190,46],"name":"src/Hydrogen/Schema/Geometry/Nurbs.purs","start":[190,1]},"title":"eqNurbsCurve"},{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Show"],"Show"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Geometry","Nurbs"],"NurbsCurve"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[195,49],"name":"src/Hydrogen/Schema/Geometry/Nurbs.purs","start":[192,1]},"title":"showNurbsCurve"}],"comments":"NURBS (Non-Uniform Rational B-Spline) curve.\n\nDegree p curve with n control points requires n + p + 1 knots.\n","info":{"dataDeclType":"newtype","declType":"data","roles":[],"typeArguments":[]},"kind":null,"sourceSpan":{"end":[188,4],"name":"src/Hydrogen/Schema/Geometry/Nurbs.purs","start":[184,1]},"title":"NurbsCurve"},{"children":[{"comments":null,"info":{"arguments":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Prim"],"Record"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["position",{"annotation":[],"contents":